From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:57:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): tell agents their context compacts on its own and
 how full it is

Subagents stopped and handed off saying their context was nearly full, judging by length alone, long before compaction. The subagent brief now says the conversation compacts on its own and to stop only when the task is done, blocked or out of iterations. Every agent also gets one line on the newest tool result at each 10% step from 50% of the window ('Context: 62% used, compacts on its own at 80%'), from the compressor's last prompt size. It is append-only and never in the system prompt, so the prompt cache holds.
